    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d288">

                <pb facs="0682" n="638" sameAs="frus:frus1946v03/pg638"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">CFM Files</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">United States Delegation Journal</hi></head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-chapter-heading" calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1946-10-03T10:00:00+01:00">October 3, 1946, 10 a.m.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#flush">USDel (PC) (Journal) 60</p>
                <p>The text of the report on the military clauses of the draft treaty with Rumania
                    was provisionally adopted.<anchor n="74" xml:id="d288-f1"/> The footnote to the
                    conclusion in the original text was deleted and an insertion made after Article
                    14 in the report. The insertion was made on a proposal by General Balmer and
                    stated that the resolution, originally proposed by the U.S. Delegation, which
                    stated that the articles on limitations in the Balkan and Finnish treaties
                    should be identical, was accepted unanimously.<anchor n="75" xml:id="d288-f2"
                    /></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d288-f1" n="74" xml:id="d288-f1-content">
                <p>For text of the report, C.P. (Plen) Doc. 18, October 5, see <ref
                        target="frus1946v04#pg_476">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">iv</hi>, p.
                        476</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d288-f2" n="75" xml:id="d288-f2-content">
                <p>Debate centered around the Soviet Delegate’s contention that article 14 of the
                    Rumanian treaty was based on article 44 of the Italian treaty. General Balmer
                    stated that it was based on article 12 of the Bulgarian treaty. See the United
                    States Delegation Journal accounts of the 14th Meeting, September 11, and the
                    28th Meeting, September 28, <ref target="#pg420">pp. 420</ref> and <ref
                        target="#pg584">584</ref>, respectively.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
